The morphe corpus (docs/design/morphe.md §13, §3.3)

Vendored inputs, provenance-tagged, exercising the formatter over real and
adversarial programs. Three trees:

- kallos/ — kallos's clingofmt-derived inputs (MIT, inputs-only, attributed;
  see kallos/LICENSE and kallos/NOTICE).
- syntax/ — a curated slice of the themelios syntax corpus (grammar corner
  seeds; see syntax/NOTICE).
- morphe/ — morphe's own adversarial cases (see morphe/NOTICE).

Classification. The corpus is clingo-dialect throughout (the ASP-Core-2
differential is later, clingo-authority work). The harness derives each input's
status by parsing it through the tier morphe trusts (§5.7): a *member* is one
the tier admits (no parse errors); a *comment-free* member carries no comment
token of any kind — trivia or `%!` documentation. Comment-bearing members are
granted too, their comments woven to the same anchors (§8); non-members are
refused (§5.7).

morphe carries no per-input expectation sidecar: the tier's parse is the
classification oracle, so member-ness and comment-freeness are read, not
restated. (Per-input sidecars carrying the dialect and member flag were
considered; deriving them from the trusted parser is equivalent for a formatter
over it, and leaner.)
